			"shows": "A metal ball lit only by an HDR sky map (no sun) at the six roughness values of the six prefiltered levels, 0 to 1 in steps of 0.2",
			"caption": "As roughness grows, the ball's reflection of the sky loses detail in steps, until only the broad light and dark of the sky remain. Roughness 0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8 and 1 (labels r0 to r1), one picture per prefiltered level.",
			"numbers": "The recipe's values: the variants r0, r02, r04, r06, r08 and r1 set the Mirror material's Roughness to 0, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 0.8 and 1. Forward.frag.slang reads the prefiltered map at level roughness * EnvironmentParams.z, so with six levels (0 to 5) each value lands on one level.",
			"alt": "Six pictures of the same metal ball in the same sky. The first mirrors the sky sharply. Each next picture is more blurred, and the last shows only a smooth gradient of light and dark.",
			"project": { "sample": "ThirdPerson" },
			"camera": { "position": [0, 1.25, 4], "target": [0, 1, 0], "fov": 20 },
			"size": [1280, 720],
			"quality": "high",
			"setup": [
				{ "command": "scene.new", "parameters": { "template": "basic3d", "force": true } },
				{ "command": "component.remove", "entityName": "Sun", "parameters": { "component": "DirectionalLight" } },
				{ "command": "component.set", "entityName": "Sky", "parameters": { "component": "SkyLight", "values": { "Source": "EnvironmentMap", "Intensity": 1.0, "EnvironmentMap": "A76F8BB1E806ACFF" } } }
			],
